Subject: [PATCH] tests: skip the CUDA architecture policy test when cross compiling

tests/cmake does not build a test binary. It installs
tests/cmake/test_cuda_architecture_policy.py into bindir as
cvcuda_test_cuda_architecture_policy, together with a copy of
cmake/CUDAArchitecturePolicy.cmake under ${datadir}/cvcuda/tests/cmake. The
script is a Python unittest that shells out to cmake to configure a series of
throwaway projects and then asserts which CUDA_ARCHITECTURES
cvcuda_configure_cuda_architecture_policy() picked for each simulated
processor. It therefore tests the build system, and only means anything on the
machine that runs the build.

When cross compiling, those two files are staged for the target image instead,
where there is no cmake and no toolchain, so every case fails with

    FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'cmake'

Adding cmake and a cross toolchain to a runtime image to satisfy a build-system
test is not reasonable, so skip the subdirectory when cross compiling.

Guarding add_subdirectory(cmake) rather than deleting the installed files
afterwards also means nvcv_add_test() is never reached for this test, so the
generated run_tests.sh driver does not gain a "run
cvcuda_test_cuda_architecture_policy cmake" line for a program that is not
present. (That driver would skip it anyway, since it treats the trailing cmake
argument as a required tool, but it is better not to reference it at all.)

Native builds are unaffected and keep running the test.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>

diff --git a/tests/CMakeLists.txt b/tests/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/tests/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tests/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -117,7 +117,16 @@ endif()
 
 # Create build tree
 
-add_subdirectory(cmake)
+if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
+    # tests/cmake installs a Python unittest that shells out to cmake to check
+    # which CUDA_ARCHITECTURES the policy function selects, plus the .cmake
+    # module it reads. That exercises the build system rather than the runtime,
+    # so when cross compiling the pair would only land in the target image,
+    # where cmake is absent and every case fails.
+    message(STATUS "Cross compiling: skipping cvcuda_test_cuda_architecture_policy")
+else()
+    add_subdirectory(cmake)
+endif()
 
 if(BUILD_TESTS_CPP OR BUILD_TESTS_PYTHON)
     add_subdirectory(common)
